  ],
  "text": "We have studied dreams for a century and still cannot agree what they are for. You spend around two hours a night doing it. Every night of your life. One theory says it is filing. The brain replaying the day to decide what to keep. Another says it is rehearsal. Running dangerous situations where nothing can actually hurt you. Notice how many dreams are being chased, or falling, or losing something. A third says it is emotional processing. Taking the sting out while keeping the memory. And the fourth says there is no purpose at all. Random signals fire in a sleeping brain, and the brain does what it always does. It builds a story. There is real evidence for all four, which is exactly why nobody has won. You will spend about six years of your life doing something nobody can explain. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
